Sure! Below is a simple example of an HTML card that rotates 180 degrees around its Y‑axis when you hover over it.  
Feel free to copy the code into an `.html` file and open it in your browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Demo</title>
<style>
/* Basic reset */
* { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }

/* Container that holds the card */
.card-wrapper {
  perspective: 1000px;          /* Gives depth to the 3D effect */
  width: 300px;
  height: 200px;
  margin: 50px auto;            /* Center horizontally */
}

/* The card itself */
.card {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  background: #fff;
  border-radius: 12px;
  box-shadow: 0 10px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
  transition: transform 0.6s ease;   /* Smooth rotation */
  transform-style: preserve-3d;      /* Needed for 3D children */
  position: relative;
}

/* Front side of the card */
.card .front,
.card .back {
  position: absolute;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  backface-visibility: hidden;      /* Hide backside when rotated */
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
  font-size: 1.5rem;
  color: #333;
  border-radius: 12px;
}

/* Back side – rotated 180° so it starts hidden */
.card .back {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);
  background: #f8f8f8;
}

/* Hover effect – rotate the whole card */
.card:hover {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
  <div class="card">
    <div class="front">
      Front Side
    </div>
    <div class="back">
      Back Side
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

1. **Perspective** – The `.card-wrapper` has `perspective: 1000px;` which gives the 3D effect a sense of depth.
2. **Transform style** – The `.card` uses `transform-style: preserve-3d;` so its children (`.front` and `.back`) keep their 3D positions.
3. **Backface visibility** – Setting `backface-visibility: hidden;` hides each side when it’s turned away from the viewer.
4. **Hover rotation** – On hover, the card rotates 180° around the Y‑axis, revealing the back side.

You can replace the text inside `.front` and `.back` with images, icons, or any other content you like. Enjoy experimenting!
